WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.300
-We're excited that you're here.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.634
-I'm happy to be here.
I'm always happy to be here.

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:04.701
-I know.
I love having you.

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:05.868
I want to talk about
this docuseries.

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:07.300
'Cause I'm --
honestly, I'm obsessed.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.968
I'm freaking out.
-It's pretty -- it's juicy.

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.367
It's good.
-It is intense.

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:13.868
But first, how is the family?
How are the little babies?

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:16.634
-They are so good.
They're keeping us so busy.

00:00:16.634 --> 00:00:19.901
They just -- Luna just turned 6,
and Miles is about to turn 4.

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:21.300
And I can't believe it.
-Come on.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.367
-Yeah.
-Is that right? Already.

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.167
-Yeah, it's so cool, though.
-6 and 4.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.801
-Yeah, but they couldn't be more
different from each other.

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.801
But it's like it keeps us
on our toes all day.

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:29.200
I truly love it.
It's so fun.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.234
-You told me that Miles is
learning how to play baseball.

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:33.300
-Yeah, he's playing
tee-ball now, which is so cool,

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.467
'cause I loved baseball
growing up, so...

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.200
-And does he understand
the rules?

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.734
-No, not at all.
-Okay, yeah.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.400
-No. He's like a blank --

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.200
I mean,
imagine going into it blindly.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.434
Like, he literally doesn't --

00:00:44.434 --> 00:00:46.300
he's never seen
a baseball game before.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.901
You'll be like -- his coach will
be like, "Go to first base,"

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:50.634
and he's like, "I don't know
what first base is!"

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:51.901
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, "I don't --" yeah.

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:54.367
-He's just a little guy.
-It's a tricky game to just

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:55.968
put on and be like, "All right,"
and try to explain

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:57.133
while it's happening.
It's too tricky.

00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:59.033
-No, it is.
And honestly, they have --

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:01.801
They have him play, like,
every different...

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.067
-Position.
-...every position.

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:05.100
And they were like,
"Miles is gonna play first,"

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.100
and I was like,
"Are you sure about that?

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.033
The ball's
always gonna go to him."

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.601
But he did, and he --
I don't know.

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:13.234
We have fun watching.
We'll say that.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:14.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.868
-You brought us a very cute clip
of Miles getting --

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:19.534
was it his first hit?
-Yeah, it was his first hit.

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:21.167
And I --
oh, my God, it was so --

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:22.534
It was really --
-So he hits the ball

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:23.667
and then doesn't quite
know what --

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:24.901
-He doesn't know what to do.
-Of course.

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:26.901
-We haven't explained it to him.
-Yeah.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.901
Here's Miles -- here's Miles
getting his first hit.

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:31.167
Look at this.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.834 --> 00:01:37.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:38.934
-He's just walking.

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:43.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:46.033
Yes!
That's Miles!

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:47.200
That's my dude!

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.601
Congratulations!

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:52.367
He was so cool.
He's like, "Now what's up?"

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:53.467
-I know, I know.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.501
We are not an athletic bunch,
honestly.

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:58.501
But John is so proud.
Someone's like, "Drop the bat!"

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:00.701
Like, you have to explain
every part.

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:02.834
Like, of course he wouldn't know
to drop the bat.

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:04.634
-No, come on.
-But it's so sweet.

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:05.901
-That's the best thing.
-It's really awesome.

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.334
-Having kids
is the greatest thing.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:09.167
-Yeah, it really is so fun.
-I heard that you had a recent

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:12.033
incident with Luna
and the Tooth Fairy.

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:13.901
-Oh, yeah.
Yeah.

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:16.267
-How does the Tooth Fairy --
I know --

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.100
-Well, I don't know the rules
of anything.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.934
Like, no one -- like, you
forget, like, what the lie is.

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:24.167
Like, at Easter, we were like --
like -- she was like, so --

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:26.200
-What's the backstory?
-Yeah, did we leave

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.734
the eggs out, or did
the Easter Bunny bring the eggs?

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:30.100
-Yeah, Easter Bunny.
-And I don't know if I'm --

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.300
Did I make the basket,

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.868
or did the Easter Bunny
make the basket?

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:34.200
-Sometimes the bunny
brings the basket.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.234
-Right?

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:36.734
-Sometimes you provide
the basket.

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:38.868
-So, it doesn't -- yeah, there's
no rhyme -- there's no rules.

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:39.901
-No rules.
-Ever.

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:41.434
-Tooth Fairy
is really out there.

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:42.868
-Tooth Fairy --
-That's a tough one to explain.

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:45.033
-Yeah.
So, she loses her first tooth,

00:02:45.033 --> 00:02:48.767
and then, I promptly
dropped it down the sink,

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:50.634
like, immediately,
in my bathroom sink.

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:52.701
And it's kind of an odd sink.
So there's this --

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:55.701
there's this, like, kind of long
divot that it could fall into.

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:58.934
And so we had to -- it was,
like, thousands of dollars.

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:00.334
-Oh, my gosh.
-We had to bring someone in

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:02.834
with a camera, like the
Roto-Rooter camera thing,

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:05.367
that goes down and spirals in.
-What?

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:07.501
-Found the tooth,
put it in a Ziploc bag.

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:08.834
I was so happy.

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:10.767
And then I threw the Ziploc bag
away, like, immediately.

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:11.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:13.267
-You totally forgot
what you're doing.

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:14.834
Like, clean it up, throw it out.
-Yeah.

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:16.901
That's my thing, too, is,
I throw away everything.

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:18.334
I love throwing things away.
-Yeah.

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:20.367
-So, yeah, that one's gone.
But I do have her other ones.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.267
-Yeah, my -- Franny swallowed
her first tooth.

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:23.501
-Oh, really?
-Yeah, she was like,

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:25.167
"I lost my first tooth."
"Oh, my God! Where is it?"

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.667
She's -- "I swallowed it."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:30.067
-Like, the root is so long.

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:32.300
I didn't know teeth roots
were that long.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:34.234
Is it just Luna?

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:36.367
-I don't know if that tooth
was ready to be pulled.

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:37.901
[ Laughter ]
-Maybe not.

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:41.067
-Really, yeah.
No, I don't think I had my --

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:43.033
I did recently, though,
my dad was giving me stuff

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.534
that he's had forever
and didn't want,

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.434
and gave me, like,
a bag of my own teeth.

00:03:47.434 --> 00:03:48.934
-See, that's --
I think that's cool!

00:03:48.934 --> 00:03:49.968
[ Laughter ]
No?

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:52.267
-No, thanks!
No, thanks!

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:54.467
-I have their umbilical cords.
-What?!

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.567
-I have --
-Yeah, I think

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.000
he gave me that, too.
It was in --

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.834
"Let's just keep it
in the shoe box. We're good."

00:03:58.834 --> 00:04:00.200
-I have the cords, teeth,
everything.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.434
-Surprise me later.
-Yeah.

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:03.067
-Yeah, I go, "No, we'll
freak out my kids later."

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:04.567
-I don't do the fingernails,
though.

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:06.501
-Oh, stop it.
No one has fingernails.

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:08.167
-No. I know, right?
-No. But I'm just like,

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:10.000
"What am I supposed to do
with my --" like, I don't know.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.100
I guess it's kind of
interesting. No.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.601
-Your old teeth?
-No.

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:14.501
-Yeah, I don't know.
My mom keeps all that stuff too.

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:15.567
-It's wild.
-Yeah.

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:16.934
-It's wild what parents keep.
-I know.

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:18.767
I don't mind it, though,
I got to say.

00:04:18.767 --> 00:04:20.534
-Yeah,
I'm good not having any --

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:21.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:23.000
I'm like --
-"I'm fine without it."

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.601
-Yeah.
You know, I was looking at

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.534
this beautiful picture
of your family.

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:27.801
Because, you guys --

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:30.467
When normal families go out,
they go to whatever.

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:32.834
They go to a restaurant,
they go bowling.

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:34.133
When you guys go out,
you go to the Grammys.

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:36.067
[ Laughter ]
-We go bowling a lot.

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:37.801
-Here's you at the Grammys.

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:39.868
Everyone looking good.

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:41.000
What was that like
to bring the kids?

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:44.601
-That was their first time
to Las Vegas.

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:46.634
-Oh, is that where it was?
-Yeah, it was crazy.

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:49.133
Because, well, John,
when he told me we were

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:51.200
gonna go to Grammys, he was
like, "Do you want to go?"

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.634
And I was like,
"Oh, it's like,

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:54.334
we're supposed to be on vacation
during this time."

00:04:54.334 --> 00:04:55.601
And then he was like, "No."

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:57.434
He's like, "Well, I've been
asked to perform," so...

00:04:57.434 --> 00:04:58.601
-He was great, by the way.

00:04:58.601 --> 00:04:59.767
-Like, "Let's bring
the whole family out."

00:04:59.767 --> 00:05:01.000
Yeah, it was really wonderful.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.300
But he didn't tell me
it was in Las Vegas.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.400
So, like, we had to bring
the whole family to Vegas.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.200
-It's usually in L.A.
-Yeah.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.701
So they had a good time, though.

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:11.200
They got to see, like, a ton
of celebrities, obviously.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.634
-But get dressed up.
And they just look like --

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:13.968
Look how cool.
-Yeah.

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:17.067
And Miles loves a suit.
He's very -- he's like John.

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:19.267
-Yeah, he's like,
"Yeah, I just hit a single.

00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:21.100
No big deal."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.634
"Now I'm off to the Grammys."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:26.200
I want to talk about this
docuseries, okay?

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.267
-Yeah.
-Now it's called "The Way Down."

00:05:28.267 --> 00:05:29.701
W-A-Y.
-Yes.

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:31.167
-And I say that because

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:34.000
didn't Gwen have a thing called,
like, "The Weigh?"

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.667
-Yeah, so she had --
she started as this --

00:05:37.667 --> 00:05:39.634
she started something called
"The Weigh Down Workshop."

00:05:39.634 --> 00:05:42.234
And she was just
this big diet guru.

00:05:42.234 --> 00:05:45.501
She was an author.
She sold a lot of books.

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:47.167
And then she re--
You know, "What do these people

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:49.968
love more than money is power."

00:05:49.968 --> 00:05:53.701
So, she kind of decided
to meld it with this, like,

00:05:53.701 --> 00:05:59.000
toxic Christianity and then
start this cult-like following

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.200
at this church called
The Remnant Fellowship.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.501
-Yeah.
Started her own church.

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:05.434
-Yes.
She preyed on the insecurities

00:06:05.434 --> 00:06:08.501
of a lot of the people
that followed her.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:11.601
And she basically had these,
you know, fundamentalist values,

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:17.434
but she tied it into, you know,
you need to pray instead of --

00:06:17.434 --> 00:06:19.434
every time you want to eat,
you should just pray.

00:06:19.434 --> 00:06:21.734
And it was basically, like,
intuitive eating.

00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:23.367
But it was just all done
so wrong and so toxic.

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:24.934
-And everyone bought this book.
And everyone got --

00:06:24.934 --> 00:06:26.033
-Everyone bought the book.

00:06:26.033 --> 00:06:27.367
Everyone was so down with
"The Weigh Down."

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:29.133
-She was on every talk show.
And it's a thing.

00:06:29.133 --> 00:06:30.300
-Yes. Yeah.
-And you're like,

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.767
"Wait. What's going on?"
-Oh, it was a big thing.

00:06:31.767 --> 00:06:33.801
Yeah, so --
And she just took off.

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:35.601
She just got
more and more powerful

00:06:35.601 --> 00:06:37.000
and had more and more followers.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.033
And everything --
the ego got bigger,

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:40.067
the hair got bigger.

00:06:40.067 --> 00:06:42.167
-Her hair, by the way,
is unbelievable.

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:44.501
-Her hair, yeah.
-You think it's a joke.

00:06:44.501 --> 00:06:45.767
It's not a joke.
-I know.

00:06:45.767 --> 00:06:47.701
You start to --
And then, I was actually like --

00:06:47.701 --> 00:06:50.033
when we were talking about this
at South by Southwest,

00:06:50.033 --> 00:06:52.067
we were trying
to figure out why.

00:06:52.067 --> 00:06:54.367
-How?
-I think it's because she wore

00:06:54.367 --> 00:06:56.567
these, like, chunky shoes
and had big hair.

00:06:56.567 --> 00:06:58.901
And I'm pretty sure
it was to make herself

00:06:58.901 --> 00:07:00.534
feel smaller, in a way.

00:07:00.534 --> 00:07:02.567
Like, if she was surrounded
by these big things,

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:04.400
it makes her feel dainty
or something.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.834
I don't know.
-I've never seen any other

00:07:05.834 --> 00:07:07.300
person with that hairdo
in my life.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:08.534
-No, never.

00:07:08.534 --> 00:07:09.701
-I don't know
what to compare it to.

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:11.000
-Higher the hair,
the closer to God, they say.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.801
-Wow -- yeah, there it is.
-Maybe that's it.

00:07:12.801 --> 00:07:15.367
-She definitely got close.

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:17.133
And the husband
and all that stuff --

00:07:17.133 --> 00:07:18.901
-Yeah.
-And then you go --

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:20.634
-Yeah, the husband was Tarzan.

00:07:20.634 --> 00:07:22.834
I mean,
it was all such a weird --

00:07:22.834 --> 00:07:25.167
-No, her husband actually was --
-He was Tarzan.

00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:26.701
-He didn't live in the jungle.
-Oh, no, sorry.

00:07:26.701 --> 00:07:28.701
He played Tarzan.
-Played Tarzan. Yeah, yeah.

00:07:28.701 --> 00:07:31.434
-Tarzan's not real?
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.434 --> 00:07:32.968
-Hopefully the kids are asleep.
They're like,

00:07:32.968 --> 00:07:34.434
"Tooth Fairy, Easter Bunny,
Tarzan."

00:07:34.434 --> 00:07:35.534
[ Laughter ]
-I know.

00:07:35.534 --> 00:07:39.000
-"What is going on?"
Tarzan is real.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.834
-Just doesn't know if he brings
his own baskets.

00:07:40.834 --> 00:07:43.501
Who knows.
-I think Joe was actually

00:07:43.501 --> 00:07:45.067
kind of the most fascinating
part of the series.

00:07:45.067 --> 00:07:46.133
-Me too!

00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:47.834
-Because he's, like,
so captivating.

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:50.567
And it's so weird.
You can totally tell this is

00:07:50.567 --> 00:07:52.400
the first time this guy's
ever opened the Bible.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.801
He's, like, reading it sideways,
and he's like trying to --

00:07:55.801 --> 00:07:58.734
-And now he's in charge.
-Yeah, and now he's the leader.

00:07:58.734 --> 00:08:00.567
-He's a leader,
and he's telling these people

00:08:00.567 --> 00:08:01.901
about this religion.

00:08:01.901 --> 00:08:03.501
Everyone's like,
"Who is this guy?"

00:08:03.501 --> 00:08:05.934
-And, you know, Natasha,
who is featured on it, as well,

00:08:05.934 --> 00:08:07.934
was his ex,
and the mother of his --

00:08:07.934 --> 00:08:10.467
-She was great.
-Yeah, she's incredible.

00:08:10.467 --> 00:08:13.367
And she just goes, she's like,
"He was never religious.

00:08:13.367 --> 00:08:16.634
He was never a religious person.
He was an out-of-work actor."

00:08:16.634 --> 00:08:18.767
And just, like,
he didn't really --

00:08:18.767 --> 00:08:20.133
This wasn't the person he was.

00:08:20.133 --> 00:08:22.367
-But it's also not
that long ago, sadly.

00:08:22.367 --> 00:08:23.734
-I know.
-I mean, like --

00:08:23.734 --> 00:08:25.467
You go, like, "Oh, is this
from the '60s or something?"

00:08:25.467 --> 00:08:27.200
And you go,
"This was like 10 years ago."

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:30.033
-That's the weirdest part to me
is, these stories exist,

00:08:30.033 --> 00:08:32.567
and we don't know about --
that this is happening.

00:08:32.567 --> 00:08:33.934
So when it was brought to me,
I was like,

00:08:33.934 --> 00:08:36.434
"No way this is happening
right now as we speak."

00:08:36.434 --> 00:08:39.701
-But can we talk about --
as you were finishing up

00:08:39.701 --> 00:08:41.834
production on the series,
something terrible happened.

00:08:41.834 --> 00:08:43.801
-Yeah, oh, my God, it was --

00:08:43.801 --> 00:08:48.200
Yeah, we woke up one day,
and just scrolling our newsfeeds

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:53.133
and saw that their -- Gwen's --
Gwen and Joe's plane

00:08:53.133 --> 00:08:56.834
had crashed into a lake
outside of Nashville,

00:08:56.834 --> 00:08:59.100
and everyone on the plane died.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.567
So, you know,
it was just like --

00:09:01.567 --> 00:09:03.200
it was terrifying
because we didn't know

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:04.767
who was on the plane exactly.

00:09:04.767 --> 00:09:07.767
And Natasha didn't know if her
daughter was on the plane.

00:09:07.767 --> 00:09:11.200
And it was just so scary
and a really weird time.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:13.901
And, you know, we'd get
on the phone with HBO Max,

00:09:13.901 --> 00:09:16.634
and we wonder, you know,
"Should we continue with this?"

00:09:16.634 --> 00:09:20.434
But then, you know, as time
passed, we realized that people

00:09:20.434 --> 00:09:22.434
were more and more okay
with speaking out

00:09:22.434 --> 00:09:23.767
now that she was gone.

00:09:23.767 --> 00:09:25.133
Like, they were very fearful
of her.

00:09:25.133 --> 00:09:26.400
-They were afraid to say
anything.

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.033
-Yeah, they were scared
to go against her.

00:09:28.033 --> 00:09:29.467
They didn't know if the church

00:09:29.467 --> 00:09:31.567
would come
and attack their families.

00:09:31.567 --> 00:09:33.934
Or, you know, they felt like
they were in danger.

00:09:33.934 --> 00:09:37.400
So, when she had passed,
people --

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:39.000
And that's kind of
what part two is,

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.734
going into it now,
are all these people

00:09:40.734 --> 00:09:43.167
that are no longer afraid
to speak out.

00:09:43.167 --> 00:09:45.400
-Oh, it is fantastic.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.834
Here's a peek of the new episode
of "The Way Down."

00:09:47.834 --> 00:09:49.167
Take a look.

00:09:49.167 --> 00:09:53.734
-That text wasn't just for
the people within Remnant

00:09:53.734 --> 00:09:55.267
but from anyone
outside of Remnant

00:09:55.267 --> 00:09:56.968
that would get ahold of that.

00:09:56.968 --> 00:10:00.133
That, I believe, was definitely
more of her motive

00:10:00.133 --> 00:10:04.067
behind that text
than it was being sent

00:10:04.067 --> 00:10:08.567
directly to
the Remnant congregation.

00:10:08.567 --> 00:10:11.200
-A lot of what cults often do
with situations like this

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:13.434
is very Orwellian.

00:10:13.434 --> 00:10:17.667
It will be almost ignored
because it does not

00:10:17.667 --> 00:10:20.667
fit their narrative
that their leader

00:10:20.667 --> 00:10:22.467
was struck down in an accident

00:10:22.467 --> 00:10:25.567
that God could have
protected her from.

00:10:25.567 --> 00:10:28.534
If the righteous are protected
by the hand of God,

00:10:28.534 --> 00:10:33.467
how could Gwen
have died like that?

00:10:33.467 --> 00:10:35.200
-Oof.
[ Applause ]

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.100
-Chrissy Teigen, everybody.
The final episodes

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:41.501
of "The Way Down: God, Greed,
and The Cult of Gwen Shamblin,"

00:10:41.501 --> 00:10:43.467
premiere Thursday on HBO Max.

